From bc2c0d8c98f51d316baeb03ce00a36e5714b731e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: benjamin <benjamin.hien@web.de>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:49:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Speed pass B1: first_attempt_full_budget switch (default off)

The heavy cells spend 20 to 60 % of all expansions on first attempts that
die at the 2 M budget and are then redone at 10 M (Benes 32 lidar-pure: 51 of
51 retries succeed). Running the first attempt at the retry budget saves that
time but is not exact: the per-window iteration cap is min(max_iterations,
remaining budget), so a larger budget can let an earlier window succeed with
a different route (gate: Benes 4x4 lidar-pure +11.7 um). Hence a switch,
measured on the 27 cells before any default changes.

Checks: fmt, clippy -D warnings, 508 core tests, 4 router-py tests, stub and
config reference regenerated, 552 Python tests, both gates exact with the
switch off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0152GWPQy8AyTgwk6GNvQ3qH
